{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '34190,34225p' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11146428\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32424507\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047036 \"A smooth muscle cell located in the middle layer of the muscularis externa of the stomach wall. This cell is arranged concentrically with the stomach's longitudinal axis, forming a continuous sheet of contractile tissue. It is fusiform in shape, containing actin and myosin filaments that enable contraction without striations. This cell contributes to the mechanical digestion and movement of food within the stomach through coordinated contractions, and plays a role in forming the pyloric sphincter in the pyloric region.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047036 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047036 \"2024-12-09T10:40:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047036 \"stomach smooth muscle circular layer cell\"@en)\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047036 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008857)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4047037 (stomach smooth muscle inner oblique layer cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29493959\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047037 \"A smooth muscle cell found in the innermost layer of the muscularis externa of the stomach wall. This cell forms a unique layer of smooth muscle fibers oriented obliquely to the stomach's longitudinal axis. It is responsible for aiding in the mixing and churning of gastric contents, contributing to mechanical digestion within the stomach.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047037 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047037 \"2024-12-09T10:53:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:ha