{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' ISSUE_COMMENTS.md && sed -n '1,260p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n\nNote for review: I did not assert the new \"interneuron of myenteric plexus\" class under existing CL:0000099, because that CL term is currently constrained to the nervous system and made the enteric/myenteric classes unsatisfiable under ROBOT reasoning. The new class is asserted as an enteric neuron with soma location in the myenteric plexus, with ascending and descending myenteric interneuron children under it.\n## Summary\n\nAdded fourteen new CL terms for issue #3584 in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`:\n\n- `CL_9900001` intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900002` interneuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900003` secretomotor/vasodilator neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900004` intestinofugal neuron\n- `CL_9900005` ascending interneuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900006` descending interneuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900007` stubby Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900008` spiny Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900009` Dogiel type II neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900010` calretinin-positive intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900011` calretinin-negative intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900012` cholinergic neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900013` nitrergic neuron of myenteric plexus\n- `CL_9900014` Dogiel type II neuron\n\n## Rationale and Modeling Notes\n\nI added definitions, PMID-backed definition xrefs, issue tracker annotations, creation dates, creator annotations, synonyms, and conservative logical axioms. Myenteric-specific terms use `has soma location` some `UBERON_0002439`. The cholinergic and nitrergic grouping classes are defined with equivalent class axioms using `capable of` some `GO_0014055` and `GO_0006809`, respectively, as requested.\n\nThe existing `CL_0000099` interneuron term is constrained with `part_of` some `UBERON_0001017` (nervous system). Asserting the new enteric/myenteric interneuron term under `CL_0000099` made `CL_9900002`, `CL_9900005`, and `CL_9900006` unsatisfiable. I therefore modeled `interneuron of myenteric plexus` as an `enteric neuron` with soma location in the myenteric plexus, and placed ascending/descending myenteric interneuron classes under that new grouping term.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- Checked existing parent terms and `dogiel type I neuron` in `cl-edit.owl`.\n- Confirmed no existing `CL_99xxxxx` terms in `cl-edit.owl`; allocated `CL_9900001` through `CL_9900014`.\n- Tried `aurelian fulltext` for the PMIDs, but `aurelian` was not installed.\n- Checked publication metadata/snippets via web search for the cited PMIDs.\n- Ran `robot convert` using a downloaded ROBOT jar in `/tmp`; passed.\n- Ran `robot reason` using the same ROBOT jar; passed after avoiding the unsatisfiable `CL_0000099` parent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
